  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Reviews Aerial Firefighting Protocols After…",
  "metaDescription": "Indonesian authorities are evaluating aerial firefighting protocols following two separate helicopter crashes during recent forest fire missions.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Two helicopters used for water bombing missions in Kalimantan crashed within a one-week period.",
    "Search and rescue teams recovered the body of a crew member involved in the Barito River incident.",
    "The Indonesian National Board for Disaster Management is currently evaluating safety procedures for aerial firefighting operations."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Within a span of one week, two helicopters involved in supporting forest and land fire suppression efforts have crashed in the Kalimantan region. The most recent incident occurred in the Barito River, resulting in the death of one crew member whose remains have been recovered and transported to Jakarta. Two other individuals involved in the same crash reportedly survived. In response to these back-to-back incidents, which included a Mi-17 V5 aircraft belonging to the military aviation center, the Indonesian National Board for Disaster Management (BNPB) and local military leadership have initiated a comprehensive evaluation of aerial firefighting protocols. Officials are investigating the operational procedures used during water bombing missions to ensure future safety for flight crews tasked with managing wildfires in the region. These accidents have prompted a broader review of the equipment and safety measures currently employed by agencies conducting wildfire mitigation activities across Indonesia.",
